WEBVTT

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:12.279
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the 31st of August. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.829
<v Callum Reid>We can hear you. Bank holiday crew, living the dream.</v>

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.760
<v Sarah Okafor>Well, there's a birthday cake in the office, so it's not entirely bleak.</v>

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.809
<v Jamie Brennan>Saw that. Someone's made a fairly engineering-sized cut in it already.</v>

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:35.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, whose new car is that in the car park? Looks far too clean to belong here.</v>

00:00:36.109 --> 00:00:40.659
<v Priya Raman>Not mine. Mine's the one with half the county on the wheel arches.</v>

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:49.549
<v Sarah Okafor>And after the charity bake sale on Friday, I think we've all had enough sugar to run a shift without the CHP.</v>

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:52.640
<v Marcus Hale>Wouldn't fancy guaranteeing the output, mind.</v>

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a catering meeting. What's finished, then what's actually ours to do?</v>

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.500
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, so I finished the repair on the GT2 bearing last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. The repair itself is closed, then?</v>

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.480
<v Priya Raman>Yep, finished. Not another repair job for today.</v>

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:21.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus Hale, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the GT2 bearing? That's the separate bit I need covered.</v>

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:27.019
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the GT2 bearing.</v>

00:01:27.819 --> 00:01:34.120
<v Priya Raman>Right, just keeping those two things distinct. My repair update wasn't me saying the permit side was sorted.</v>

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:39.239
<v Marcus Hale>Understood. Permit to work and isolation are with me; not repeating your repair.</v>

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Other completed bits?</v>

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:49.870
<v Hannah Price>I already swapped the filter on the Gas Turbine 1 yesterday. That's off the list.</v>

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:55.390
<v Callum Reid>Yep, heard that on handover. No outstanding filter change there.</v>

00:01:57.769 --> 00:02:04.420
<v Fiona Doyle>And I tested the boiler feed pump yesterday and it's all fine now. That's a completed one as well.</v>

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:11.370
<v Callum Reid>Good. Nice to have a few things in the done column for once.</v>

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:18.930
<v Jamie Brennan>Just an observation from nights: noticed the fire alarm panel was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.610
<v Priya Raman>Settled down during nights, you mean? Not still doing it?</v>

00:02:24.919 --> 00:02:29.819
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, settled down then. Nothing ongoing in that report; I'm not raising another job.</v>

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:35.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation noted, not an action coming out of this stand-up.</v>

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:44.539
<v Hannah Price>Other thing from me, I'm still waiting on parts for the boiler safety valve. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.520
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, those parts aren't here. No change to that blocker.</v>

00:02:51.759 --> 00:02:58.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, boiler safety valve stays blocked. Not putting it down as work somebody can get on with today.</v>

00:02:58.789 --> 00:03:06.139
<v Callum Reid>On the live stuff, the guarding on the line 3 needs checking. That's the one I wanted to bring up first.</v>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.710
<v Hannah Price>I'll check the guarding on the line 3. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. Agreed, straight away for the guarding on the line 3.</v>

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.750
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's not one for the bottom of the list.</v>

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.900
<v Hannah Price>No, absolutely. That's my first one.</v>

00:03:27.259 --> 00:03:30.409
<v Sarah Okafor>And where are we with the line 2 robot?</v>

00:03:31.979 --> 00:03:40.030
<v Callum Reid>Still got the jam. It needs clearing, and the sensors need checking as part of that. Not just the jam on its own.</v>

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:48.900
<v Hannah Price>I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot this morning. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:49.919 --> 00:03:55.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Hannah, both parts of that this morning. Fairly important, with the safety-critical guarding still first.</v>

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:02.099
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that's the order I've got. Guarding straight away, then the line 2 robot this morning.</v>

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:09.030
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, I talked over the end there—Teams did its little underwater thing. You said sensors as well?</v>

00:04:09.919 --> 00:04:13.770
<v Callum Reid>She did, yeah. Clear the jam and check the sensors. Both.</v>

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:19.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Next one is the sensors on the dryer.</v>

00:04:20.279 --> 00:04:24.829
<v Marcus Hale>I'll recalibrate the sensors on the dryer by the end of the week.</v>

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:30.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marcus. Recalibrate the sensors on the dryer, by the end of the week. Agreed.</v>

00:04:32.649 --> 00:04:34.050
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, that's with me.</v>

00:04:35.939 --> 00:04:41.540
<v Fiona Doyle>End of the week, got it. Not putting that into the straight-away bucket with the guarding.</v>

00:04:43.879 --> 00:04:48.079
<v Jamie Brennan>And the seals on the MV01—is that still one we're agreeing here?</v>

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:53.170
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the MV01 by the 28th. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:54.189 --> 00:04:59.790
<v Fiona Doyle>Just flagging the date wording: we're on the 31st, so the 28th is already behind us.</v>

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:09.290
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that's the deadline on it. I'm not moving it to a different date here. I'll take the seal replacement, still normal priority.</v>

00:05:10.079 --> 00:05:19.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Marcus Hale owns replacing the seals on the MV01. Keep 'by the 28th' as the stated deadline and normal priority; we're not quietly rewriting either.</v>

00:05:21.019 --> 00:05:25.569
<v Callum Reid>Right, so that date query isn't us suddenly calling it an urgent job.</v>

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.670
<v Marcus Hale>Exactly. Normal priority for the MV01 seals.</v>

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:38.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Quick read-back, then. Marcus Hale, permit to work and isolation for the GT2 bearing, separate from the repair Priya's already finished.</v>

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:39.970
<v Marcus Hale>Yes, accepted. That's mine.</v>

00:05:42.089 --> 00:05:51.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, guarding on the line 3 straight away, safety critical; clear the jam and check the sensors on the line 2 robot this morning, fairly important.</v>

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:57.240
<v Hannah Price>Yep, both agreed. And the boiler safety valve is still blocked, not a third live job.</v>

00:05:57.629 --> 00:06:04.279
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, the sensors on the dryer by the end of the week. We've already pinned down the MV01 wording.</v>

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:12.199
<v Fiona Doyle>All matches what I've got. Completed items and the blocked valve are separate from those actions.</v>

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:16.709
<v Priya Raman>Nothing else from electrical. And yes, you all sound normal again now.</v>

00:06:17.459 --> 00:06:19.560
<v Jamie Brennan>That's generous. Audio might be normal.</v>

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:28.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that'll do us. Thanks, everyone. Hopefully there's still some birthday cake left when we get off Teams.</v>

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.040
<v Callum Reid>Depends how long your goodbye takes. Cheers, all.</v>
